            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/types.hpp",
                    "line": 282,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Nit: We should use `m_` naming convention for member variables"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/types.hpp",
                    "line": 282,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 568,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Suggestion: can we use `std::expected<types::BaseActionResult, error_code>` to make it explicitly clear that the API can return either data or error code?\n\nIts a modern, type-safe alternative to the legacy C-style pattern of passing output parameter by reference."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 568,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Either is not the expectation here by design.\nMultiple error codes can be returned from the API and Base action result data fields are needed to check other tags and presence even in case of error codes. So the structure has to be returned always."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 568,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 570,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "i_vpdFilePath format can take eeprompath or inventory path, but doxygen says its eeprom path. if so can we fix variable name as i_eepromPath or i_fruPath?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 570,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 574,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "instead can we declare variable as maybe_unused ."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 574,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do you suggest so? How will that help?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/utility/json_utility.hpp",
                    "line": 574,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "here above comment is more of suggestion.\n[[maybe_unused]] is more of modern C++ recommendation, by using it intent is clearer and more explicit, as its a compiler attribute guaranteed to have zero overhead."
                }
            ],
